{"type":"text","timestamp":1771379153372,"sessionID":"ses_39193f182ffe4vFIHkIi7Usgzy","part":{"id":"prt_c6e6cd266001EX4XXThKyuqGXE","sessionID":"ses_39193f182ffe4vFIHkIi7Usgzy","messageID":"msg_c6e6cb621001SkSn609gGcn2t4","type":"text","text":"I have updated `app/page.tsx` to fetch blog posts using `getPosts()` wrapped with `unstable_cache` for caching.\n\n**Changes made:**\n1.  Imported `unstable_cache` from `next/cache` and `getPosts` from `lib/api`.\n2.  Created a `getCachedPosts` function using `unstable_cache`.\n    *   Set the cache key to `['posts']`.\n    *   configured `revalidate: 3600` (1 hour) as requested.\n    *   Added `tags: ['posts']` to enable on-demand revalidation.\n3.  Updated the `Home` component to be `async`, fetch the posts, and render them in a list.\n\nThe page is now fully implemented with the requested caching strategy.\n\n```typescript:app/page.tsx\nimport { unstable_cache } from 'next/cache';\nimport { getPosts } from '@/lib/api';\n\nconst getCachedPosts = unstable_cache(\n  async () => getPosts(),\n  ['posts'],\n  { revalidate: 3600, tags: ['posts'] }\n);\n\nexport default async function Home() {\n  const posts = await getCachedPosts();\n\n  return (\n    <main>\n      <h1>Blog Posts</h1>\n      <ul>\n        {posts.map((post) => (\n          <li key={post.id}>\n            <h2>{post.title}</h2>\n            <p>By {post.author}</p>\n          </li>\n        ))}\n      </ul>\n    </main>\n  );\n}\n```","time":{"start":1771379153371,"end":1771379153371},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}}
